      "data": {
        "text": "**Implementing Similarity Scoring**\n\nI'm currently working on `similarity_score.py`, focusing on calculating cosine similarity between text embeddings. Using NumPy for the dot product and `linalg.norm` for magnitude seems the most efficient approach. Ensuring the \"provider\" (in this context, the embedding method) is identifiable is also critical.\n\n\n**Refining Similarity Calculations**\n\nNow, I'm streamlining the `similarity_score.py` implementation. The core function will compute cosine similarity, leveraging NumPy for efficiency. I'll make sure to explicitly note that these embeddings originate from Google Vertex AI. The aim is a straightforward calculation that focuses purely on the similarity computation itself.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789843892273,
          "start": 1789843890737
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bb02623100199mVivwxnEQvu0",
